# Feature catalog sync

Whenever you **add**, **remove**, **rename**, or **materially change** a user-facing feature (including Settings toggles, menus, Web Editor, player/PiP, ads/YouTube hooks, Spaces/locks, Premium gates), update [`docs/XBrowser-Feature-Catalog.md`](docs/XBrowser-Feature-Catalog.md) in the **same task**.

## What to update

- Add or revise the matching row under **Core** or **Non-core** with a one-line description.
- If Premium gating changes, update the Premium section and the “future Premium expansion” notes.
- Keep entries concrete (prefer “YouTube video ad auto-skip” over a vague bucket).
- Do not invent marketing claims; describe what the product actually does.
- UI-facing names in the catalog may stay English to match the app.

## When it does not apply

- Pure refactors, bugfixes with no user-visible behavior change, build/Pods-only, or docs-only unrelated to features.

## Done check

Before finishing feature work, confirm the catalog reflects the new or changed capability (or explicitly note why no catalog change was needed).
